We discuss in detail the reconstruction of the AMOC transport index ψψ in iCESM. First, the 5 paleo AMOC-sensitive indicators that can be represented in iCESM are interpolated to yearly data; these 5 indicators consist of three involving stable water isotopes (the δδ18O difference cross Florida Strait12, the δδ18ONPS-Tq at south Greenland margin10,20, and the δδ18O near Laurentia Channel16) and two related to ocean temperatures (the dipole pattern of SPG subsurface ocean temperature14 and the warming hole index6) (“Method 1”). These 5 proxies, which are denoted by \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
